  "goodToKnow": "Die Wasserversorgung is the water supply. In Germany, it's mostly run by municipal utilities (Stadtwerke), and tap water (Leitungswasser) is among the most strictly controlled foodstuffs under the Trinkwasserverordnung. Still, restaurants rarely serve free tap water, and Germans love sparkling mineral water (Sprudel). Die Versorgung means supply or care: die Stromversorgung, die medizinische Versorgung. It has no plural."
